 National Teams Analysis Page
Overview & Purpose
This page provides a detailed comparative evaluation of team performances across the tournament, highlighting top-performing squads, underperforming teams, and goal metrics across groups.

Key Insights
Top Performers & Defensive Efficiency: France, the Netherlands, and Germany demonstrated superior attacking firepower. Concurrently, Argentina established the strongest defensive resilience, conceding only 1 goal throughout their campaign.

Underperforming Teams: Teams at the bottom of the rankings struggled significantly in defensive organization, conceding up to 12 goals while failing to secure points.

Group Dynamic Variations: Goal distribution across groups varied noticeably, with Groups 2, 6, and 9 exhibiting the highest scoring density.

Consistency in Victory: Argentina, Mexico, and France maintained the highest conversion rates from matches played to total points won.
